  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the end of three years from the date of this permission. \r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\r Flood Risk Assessment (Dated December 2025),\r SuDS Pro Forma,\r Highway Safety Impact Form,\r E00 (Dated 19/11/2025),\r E01 (Dated 19/11/2025),\r E02 (Dated 19/11/2025),\r E03 (Dated 19/11/2025),\r E04 (Dated 19/11/2025),\r P00 (Dated 30/01/2026),\r P01 (Dated 30/01/2026),\r P02 (Dated 30/01/2026),\r P03 (Dated 30/01/2026),\r P04 (Dated 30/01/2026),\r P05 (Dated 30/01/2026).\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.",
    "All new external work shall be carried out in materials that resemble, as closely as possible, in colour and texture as specified in the approved application.\r\rReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area.",
    "The HMO hereby permitted shall not be occupied by more than 6 residents at any one time, unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority. \r \rReason: To ensure that the future occupation of the building does not compromise standards of accommodation and does not adversely affect the residential amenities of neighbouring properties.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms and the ground floor communal kitchen and dining room, and the first floor communal kitchen shall be retained in perpetuity. \r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r"
  ],
